10. Powerc and Duties ofthe Rector:
The Rector shall be the principal executive academic officers of the Institute(llMS) and shall be responsible for the implementation of the provisions of theAct, the statutes, the regulations and the rules and execution of the polic:iesand programs of the lnstitute (llMS).The Rector may, in an emergency which in his opinion requires immediateaction, take such action as he may consider necessary and shall, as soonthereafter as possible, report his action to the officer, authority or other brldywhich in the ordinary course, would have dealt with the matter.The Rector shall, in the absence of the Pro-Chancellor' preside over themeetings of the Authorities of which the Pro-Chancellor is the Chairman.Exercise and perform such other powers and functions as may be prescribt:d.
