The Board of Advanced Studies and Research;The Finance and planning committee;Discipline committee; andSuch other authorities as may be prescribed by the statutes
17. .The Board of Governors:
(a)
(b)
The Board of Governors shall consist of:The Rector shall be its chairman.(a) The chief justice of the high court of Pakistan (lslamabad) orjudge of the High court nominated by him-(b) Tw6 memberJ of the National assembly of Pakistan to benominated by the National assembly of Pakistan'(c)Vice-Chancellors,ortheirnominees,ofPublicSectorlnstituteofPakistan.(d) Secretary of the Government of Pakistan, Education andprofessional training Department;(e) bne or more deanl to be appointed by the Chancellor on therecommendation of the ComPanY.(f) Two members of outstanding merit nominated by the Company;ijl f*o members of outstanding merit to be nominated by the bar(h) F""i,i?;rr.ns of eminence representing various disciplines and' ' profession nominated by the Rector on recommendation of theof board of faculties;(i) Chairman Higher Education commission or his nominee;i;i fwo members nominated by the Company from BoD;(i) eresident Chamber of commerce and lndustry;(l) The Registrar who shall act as its secretary'Memberoftheboardotherthanex-officiomembersshallholdofficeforthree years and shall be eligible for re-nomination.
18. Powers & Duties of the Board:
(ii)(iii)
The board shall be the executive board and under the provisions of thisAct.Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing powers, and subjectto the proviiions of this Act and the statutes and the board shall havetthe powers to:-Hold control and administer the property and funds of the lnstitute(ilMS);boruin and regulate, with due regard to the advice of the finance andplanning committees the finances, accounts investments of theinstitute (llMS) and for that purpose, to appoint such agents as it nlaybe fit;Consider annual/revised budget estimates and to advise the Companythereon, and to re-appropriate funds from one head to another'
(iv)(v)
(vi)
