Transfer and accept, transfer of movable or immovable property onbehalf of the lnstitute (llMS);Enter into, vary, carry out and cancel on behalf of the Institute (llMS);Cause proper books of accounts to be kept for all sums of moneyreciev'ed and expended by the lnstitute (lltt/S) and for the assets andliabilities of the tnstitute (llMS);Receive and manage any property transferred and grants, bequests,donations, endowments and other contributions made to the lnstitute(ilMS);Administer funds placed at the disposal of the lnstitute (llMS) forspecified purposes;Determine the form, provide for the custody and regulate the use of thecommon seal of the lnstitute (llMS);Provide the buildings, libraries, premises, furniture, .apparatus,equipment and other means required for carrying out the work of thelnstitute (llMS);Establish and maintain halls of residence and hostels or approve orIicense hostels and lodgings for the residence of students.lnstitute professorship, Associate professorship, AssistantProfessorship, Lectureship and other teaching posts or to suspend orabolish such posts;To affiliate, associate, collaborate, enlist, constitute, takeover, declareand disaffiliate, disassociate, no collaborate, duelist and undeclared,educational institutions, organizations, association, bodies andcolleges;Create, suspend or abolish such administrative, teaching, research orother posts as may be necessary.Make appointments on recommendation of the selection board to theposts of teachers, officers bnd such others may be determined;Confer honorary degrees in accordance with the conditions prescribed;Prescribe duties of officers/teachers and other employees of thelnstitute (llMS);Appoint Emeritus and distinguish professors on such terms andconditions as may be prescribed;Suspend, punish and remove from service officers (other than theRector), teachers and other employees in the manner prescribed;Appoint members of the various authorities in accordance with theprovisions of this Act.Propose statutes for submission of the Chancellor;Consider and dispose of the regulations made by the academic,provided that the board may frame a regulation on its own initiative andapprove it after consulting the academic council.Regulate, determine and administer all other matters concerning thelnstitute (llMS), and to this end, exercise all other powers notspecifically mentioned in this act and the statutes.Delegate any of its powers to an Authority or officer or a committee thesub committee and
