20.
21. Academic Council:
22. Powers and Academic council:
(a)
The Academic council shall be the highest academic body of thelnstitute (llMS), and shall subject to the provisions of this Act and thestatutes , have powers to lay down proper standards of instruction,scholarship, research and examinations, and to regulate and promotethe academic life of the lnstitute (llMS);ln particular and without prejudice to the generality of the foregcingprovisions, the council shall have the power to:
(i) Advise the board on academic matters.
Meeting of the board:(a) The Board shall meet at least two times in a year. Dates of meetingare to be fixed by the Vice-Chancellor. Special meetings rrayhowever be called at any time on the direction of the board or on arequisition made by not less than four members of the Board toconsider a matter of urgent nature-(b) Not less than ten clear days' notice of a special meeting s.nall pegiven to the members and the agenda of the meeting shall beiestricted to the matter for which the special meeting is called.(c) The quorum for a meeting of the board shall be once half of itsmembers, a fraction being counted as one.(d) The decision of the board shall be expressed in terms of the viewsof the majority of the members present and voting and, if 'themembers are equally divided, the Chairman of the board shall haveand exercise a casting vote.
(a) The academic council shall consist of:(i) The Rector who shall be the Chairman;(ii) The Deans(iii) The Directors(iv) Institute (llMS) Professors including Emeritus andDistinguished Professors(v) The Chairman of the teaching departments(vi) Five eminent persons known for their intellectual caliberon international level , service to TrusUSocie$/Companyor leadership in profession nominated by the chancelloron the recommendation of the Rector;(vii) The controller of examinationiviii) ftre librarian(ix) The registrar who shall act as a secretary.
(b)
