To regulate the admission of students to the courses ofstudies and examinations;Propose to the board, Schemes for the constitution andorganization of teaching departments institutes andfaculties;To consider or formulate proposals for the planning anddevelopment of teaching and research and in the lnstitute(ilMS);To make regulations on the recommendations of theBoard of faculties and the Board of Studies prescribingthe course of studies and the syllabi for all lnstitute (llMS)examinations; Provided that, if the recommendations ofboard of faculties and board of studies are not receivedby the prescribed date, and the council may, subject tothe approval of the boaid, continue for the next year thecourses of studies already prescribed;To recognize the Examination of other lnstitute (llMS) orexamining body as equivalent to the correspondingexaminations of the lnstitute (llMS);To frame regulations for submissions to board.To appoint members to the various authorities inaccordance with the provisions of this ordinance and;To p6rform such other functions as may be prescribed bythe statutes.
GHAPTER VI
STATUTES REGULATIONS AND RULES
Subject to the provisions of this Act. Chancellor may make/promulgatestatutes to regulate or prescribe all or any of the following matters namely-(a) Terms and conditions of service, including pay, constitution of pension ,insurance , gratuity , provident fund , benevolent fund and other fringebenefits,(b) Terms and conditions of conttractual appointments;(c) Establishment of Faculties and other academic units and divisions;(d) Affiliation and Disaffiliation of institutions and related matters;(e) Powers and duties of officers and teachers;if) Conditions under which the lnstitute (llMS) may enter into arrangementswith other organizations for purposes of instruction , research and otherrcl3J"ti'Y.3ttuJ''3"ooo,n,r"nt of Professor Emeritus and DistinsuishedProfessors;(h) Award of honorary degrees(i1- Standards for evaluation of efficiency and exercising disciplinary measuresover the employees of the lnstitute (llMS)
