When a member of a newly constituted Authority is appointed ornominated, the term of office, as fixed under this Act, shall commencefrom such date as may be prescribed.
31. Filling of casual vacancies in Authorities:
(a) Any casual vacancy among the appointed or nominated members ofany Authority shall be filled as soon as conveniently may be, by theperson or the body who appointed or nominated the member whoseplace has become vacant.(b) The person appointed or nominated to the vacancy shall be a memberof such Authority for the residue of the term for which the personwhose place he fills would have become a member provided that:1. Where a vacancy in the membership of an Authority, other thanthe Board cannot be filled for the reason that the member wasex- officio, and the office has ceased to exist.2. Or the organization, institution or other body, other than thelnstitute (llMS) has ceased to exit or has ceased to function3. Or for any other circumstances, which make it impractible to fillthe vacancy, the vacancy shall be filled in such manner theChancellor may direct on the recommendations of the Board.(C) The officer of a nominated member shall become vacant if he resignsor fails to attend the three consecutive meetings of the Authoritywithout sufficient cause or leave of absence, or his nomination ischanged by the nominating Authority.
32. Disputes about membership of Authority:
(a) Not withstanding anything containe in this Act, a person nominated orappointed in any Authority shall cease to be a member of suchAuthority as soon as he has ceased to hold the position by virtue ofwhich he was nominated or appointed.(b) If a question arises whether any person is entitled to be a member ofany Authority, the matter shall be referred to a committee consisting ofthe Rector, the judge of the high court of Pakistan or member of highcourt bar council Pakistan, who is the member of the board and anominee of the TrusVsociety/Company and the decision of thecommittee shall be final and binding.
33. Constitution, Functions and powers of other Authority:
The constitution, function and power of other authority for which nospecific provision or insufficient provision has been made in this Act,shall be such as may be prescribed by the statutes.
34. Appointment of committee by the Authority:
tZ
The board, The Academic council or other Authorities may appointsuch standing, Special or Advisory committee, as they may consideradvantages in the performance of their functions.

endstream
