There shall be a teaching department for each subject or a group ofsubjects as may be prescribed by the regulations and each teachinEldepartment shall be headed by Chairman.The chairman of a teaching department shall be appointed by theBoard on the recommendation of the Rector from amongst the threermost senior Professors and three mosl senior Associate Professors ofthe department for a period of three years.Provided that where there is no Professor or Associate professor in adepartment, it shall be looked after by the Dean of .the faculty with theassistance of the most senior teacher of the department'Chairman of the Department shall plan, organize and supervise thework of the department and shall be responsible to the Dean for thework of this department.
There shall be a separate board of studies for each subject or group ofsubjects as may be prescribed by the regulations.Each board of studies shall consist of:(i) The chairman of the Department who shall act its chairman and
5
conveyor.(ii) All professor and associate professors in the Department or theinstitute;(iii) Three teachers other than the lnstitute (lltt/S) teachers to beappointed by the Faculty Board. The number will be determinedOy tne facuity board according to the needs of each Board and;(iv) Three experts to be appointed by the Rector'Function of the Board of Studies shall be to:
To advice the authorities on all academic matters connected withinstructions, research and examination in the subject or subjectsconcerned.To purpose curricula and syllabi for all degrees diplomas andcertificate courses in the subject or subject concerned;To suggest a panel of names of paper setters and examiners in thesubject or subject concerned and;To perform such other functions as may be prescribed by theregulations.
