6. The Board of Advance Studies and Research:
(a) The Advanced studies and research Board shall consist of;(0 The Rector who shall be the Chairman,(ii) The Deans.(iii) Three lnstitute (llMS) Professors other than Deans.(iv) Three scholars of eminence in a field not represented on theBoard of Advanced Studies and Research.
7. The Functions ofthe Advanced Studies and Research Board shall be:
(a)(b)
To advice the authorities on all matters connected with the promotionof Advance studies and research in the lnstitute (llMS);To consider and report to the Authorities on the institution of researchdegree in the lnstitute (llMS);To appoint supervisors for research studies;To appoint supervisors for research studies;To recommend the name of examiners for the research degrees.
(c)(d)(e)
8
The selection board:(a) There shall be the selection board consisting of:
(a) Rector (Chairperson);iui oean oithe Faculty Concerned;(c) Head ofthe Department Concerned;(d) Two Members of the Board to be nominated by the Board ofGovernors;(e) One Eminent Scholar to be nominated by the Board ofGovernors;(f) Director QEC; and(g) Registrar (Secretary of the Selection Board).
Member of board, other than ex-officio members, shall hold office forthree years;The quorum for a meeting of the selection board shall be fivemembers;No member of the selection board who is a canditate for the post towhich appointment to be made shall take part in such proceedings ofthe Board;ln selecting candidates as professors and associate professor, theselection board shall co-opt three experts in the subject concerned. lnselecting candidates for other teaching posts, two experts in thesubject concerned. The experts will be nominated by the Rector, from astanding list of experts approved by the Board on recommendations ofSelection board.
10. The function of the Selection Board shall be to:
(b)(c)(d)
(e)
